  "goodToKnow": "Die Auferstehung is resurrection, especially of Jesus, celebrated at Easter (Ostern). Easter Monday is a public holiday in Germany, as is Good Friday (Karfreitag), when dance events are banned in many states (Tanzverbot). Figuratively, it's a revival or comeback: die Auferstehung einer Marke. The GDR anthem began Auferstanden aus Ruinen (risen from ruins). Mahler's Second Symphony is called the Auferstehungssinfonie. It has no plural."
